invariant: INV-26
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: AES=soft stops being one implementation and adds the hardware one
  beside it, so a TRANSPORT=quic-nonblocking AES=soft object carries two definitions
  of aes_expand_round_keys and aes_cipher_block. The rule is the one PIN
  keeps: one implementation per object, chosen by a build variable, never
  two. The linker would refuse this particular pair, but a linker is not
  the gate — it says nothing about which implementation an object ended
  up with, and an object that quietly carried the table cipher while its
  build line said AES=hw would still link. The lint reads the packaged
  source list per axis value, so it names the file that does not belong.

--- old
AES_IMPL := quic_aes_soft.c
--- new
AES_IMPL := quic_aes_soft.c quic_aes_hw.c
